course: dictionary
lesson: 3606
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word fight can mean to hurt someone, to argue angrily, or to try very hard to get or stop something. «The body raises its temperature to fight infection.» Here fight means to try very hard to stop something, not to hit anyone.
explain: Look at the words around it. «You never kick or throw a ball at someone who is not ready, because it hurts and starts fights.» The word hurts tells you fights here means people hurting each other, and that is never the way to solve a problem. Walk away, use words, or get an adult.
explain: Fight can also be a noun, a thing you can have. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it: if «They had an argument at lunch» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Fight can be a verb: fight, fights, fought, fighting.
fact: Fight can also be a noun: a fight, fights.
fact: «Fight» can mean to try very hard to get or stop something, as in «fight a fire» or «fight an illness».
fact: Common phrases include «fight back», «fight for», «fight off» and «put up a fight».
fact: Fighting with fists is never the way to solve a problem: walk away, use words, or get an adult.
exercise: «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection.» What does fight mean here? | To argue angrily | To run away | *To try very hard to stop something | To hit someone with fists
exercise: «You never kick or throw a ball at someone who is not ready, because it hurts and starts fights.» What is a fight in this sentence? | A big bag of balls | *A hurtful clash between people | A school trip | A kind game of catch
exercise: «They had a fight about whose turn it was.» Which word is a noun in this sentence? | whose | *fight | about | had
test: «Doctors fight illness, and firefighters fight fires.» What does fight mean in both places? | To argue angrily | To hit someone | *To try very hard to stop something | To put on a show
test: Ella says, «Fight is only ever about hitting people.» Why is she wrong? | Fight is a noun, so it cannot hit people | Fight only means to win a game | Fight means to run and hide | *Fight can also mean to try very hard to stop something, like fighting an illness
exam: At the yearly check-up, «a dog gets a vaccine that teaches its body to fight dangerous illnesses before it ever meets them»: what does fight mean? | To sleep deeply | To hit another dog | To argue angrily | *To be ready to stop something harmful
